    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: cevas-theorem-oq-02-oq-01\n\nInsights accumulated during research on this problem.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThe problem concerns a spherical version of Ceva's theorem expressed through unit vectors in an inner product space. Cevian points on arcs are defined by normalizing weighted sums such as α·B + β·C. The stated target relates spherical arc sine ratios to the corresponding weight ratios and reduces the concurrency condition to α_D α_E α_F = β_D β_E β_F.\n\n---\n\n## Insights\n\n- The single-cevian ratio is stated as sin(BD) / sin(DC) = β / α.\n- The three cevian ratios multiply to the product of the corresponding weight ratios.\n- The spherical Ceva concurrency condition is stated as α_D α_E α_F = β_D β_E β_F.\n\n---\n\n## Dead Ends\n\nNo dead ends are recorded in the local knowledge file.\n"
